      "description": "These were camps established by Nazi Germany for the imprisonment, forced labor, and extermination of Jews and other groups deemed undesirable. The striped uniforms and barbed wire in the image are iconic symbols of these camps, which are not explicitly labeled but are essential to understanding the historical context.",
